00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:33.190 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  to better understand where the story of  halo infinite begins let's have a brief  recap of where we're at with the  reclaimer saga  during the events of halo 4 the ancient  forerunner known as the didact has  returned  [Music]  having been locked up in stasis for  thousands of years he still blames  humanity for the wars of the past  master chief is able to defeat didact  and his army of prometheans  but loses cortana in the process as she  uses the last of her power to protect  the chief from the detonation of a  nuclear bomb  [Music]  in halo 5 master chief discovers that  cortana is still alive  she used 4runner technology to survive  and expand across the galaxy  with her rejuvenation she intends to  bring peace to the universe  and believed that it was up to the  created ais to protect it  cortana calls on all ai throughout the  galaxy to assist in her goal  as well as reactivating ancient  forerunner weapons called guardians  she plans on using them to forcibly  bring peace to the planets  regardless of whether the occupants want  it or not  to cortana and the created this may seem  like the most logical approach  but for sentient races this essentially  means the removal of free will  master chief goes rogue in an attempt to  save her and talk her into standing down  while the unsc concerned that master  chief is being manipulated by the ai  sends an escort of spartans to bring him  back  halo 5 ends with cortana humming to  herself while appearing to activate one  of the halo rings  the halo infinite campaign begins near  the damaged halo installation known as  sita halo  after a stranded unsc soldier known as  the pilot  saves master chief from being sucked out  into space the pilot goes on to tell the  chief of a recent unsc defeat  with heavy damage to the ring world it  would appear that the unsc were engaged  in a conflict between the banished  returning as an enemy faction from halo  wars 2 and potentially the created  on top of this mask chief has also  discovered the weapon a cortana-like ai  who claims that the original cortana was  deleted after infiltrating sita halo  however the chief city hadn't deleted  her but also there was a built-in  subroutine that was designed to delete  the weapon once cortana was gone adding  a further amount of ambiguity to the  situation  at this stage it appears that the story  of halo infinite will be centered around  taking down the banished forces on zeta  halo and uncovering the mystery around  cortana and the weapon  it's likely that the unsc plus various  others will be looking to destroy  cortana  but as in halo 5 master chief will be  attempting to stop her without going to  those extremes  if possible  given the number of races affected by  cortana's plans it's also possible that  the master chief will be fighting more  than just a couple of different factions  this time  there is the potential for quite a  number of different groups making their  way to zeta to put a stop to the ai who  has threatened to take control of the  galaxy  there has been quite a bit of concern  around the open world concept that was  announced people fear that it will  become a ubisoft or even a destiny clone  in the way that they manage it  but from what i've been able to check  out it's far from this  in fact i would goes far to say that  this feels much more like a classic halo  campaign than we've seen in many many  years  just on a much much larger scale  i felt the same sort of vibes that i had  with the original game all those years  ago  the game starts with master chief crash  landing on zeta halo  it has been months since the unsc forces  lost the conflict that took place  and the banished now control the  majority of the ring planet  the chief's job is to secure and bring  the unsc soldiers who are spread across  the map together and recapture ground  for humanity  there were forward operating bases  across the land that are now under  banished control  capturing these will provide resources  like weapons and equipment but also the  ability to fast travel and summon  vehicles  while there is still a clear mission  direction marker there are a number of  smaller conflicts and objectives around  the map  these are outside of the main missions  but will often have a named enemy within  that needs to be taken out  these enemies will not only have some  background law but specialized weaponry  that can be collected  it's up to the player as to whether they  would like to push through the missions  or explore the entire map rescuing  soldiers capturing forward operating  bases and taking down named enemies  some missions certainly feel more linear  with tighter bases and funnel points but  even in this situation everything just  feels much larger and more epic  speaking of which remember in the  original game when you'd come across  unsc soldiers and they would tag along  and help out  this would usually only be for short  bursts as the mission structure would  usually cut them off  but this isn't the case in infinite  there is a seemingly limitless supply of  soldiers dotted around that constantly  respawn especially around the captured  forward operating bases  i'm kind of keen to see how many i can  bring together at once and watch how  they handle a large conflict  love him or hate him halo will be  following the battle pass trend of other  shooters in the market  they have stated that this isn't working  as intended right now and while we've  seen a few adjustments to this recently  i have a feeling we'll be seeing a few  more in the coming weeks  each battle pass season will last for  three months with week-long events  dotted throughout  the seasons are how you unlock new gear  and customization options  fortunately if you miss a season or  didn't manage to complete it you have  the option to go back and work on past  tracks  halo infinite will not launch with a  co-op campaign or forge mode  rather than delay the game again they've  decided to bring these out when they're  ready to be released  we shouldn't expect to see the co-op  until at least may 2022  and forge another three months after  that  but as always the divs have warned that  these dates are only goals  these could potentially shift again if  other priorities come up  most people will be aware of this but i  have to chuck it in there halo infinite  multiplayer is free to play in cross  platform with cross progression across  xbox one xbox series x and pc  the halo open world will also be getting  a day night cycle obviously not one of  the most major of additions but it's the  little things that count  for the immersion of the world this is a  good step to take and will help it feel  a bit more alive  and last but certainly not least this  will be the last standalone halo title  for at least the next 10 years  343 industries has no plans to make any  other standalone halo titles in the  future instead infinite will act as a  platform to further halo experiences  chrisley explains  halo infinite is the start of our  platform for the future  we want infinite to grow over time  versus going into those numbered titles  and having all that segmentation that we  had before  it's really about creating halo infinite  as the start of the next 10 years for  halo and then building that as we go  with our fans and the community  i hadn't originally planned to dive into  halo infinite but i've been having a  hell of a lot of fun with the  multiplayer up until now  plus the other games i covered just  really haven't got a lot going on at the  moment i actually really didn't want to  try this halo as i didn't actually enjoy  some of the more recent games it was  affecting some of the good memories i  had from the early days of the franchise  but i'm so glad i did because this is  looking to be shaping up into something  special  so while i'll still be covering the  other games with the infinite campaign  coming out on the 8th of december i  already know i'm going to be putting in  some serious hours  so expect to see more videos coming out  in the future  anyway i hope you're looking forward to  it as much as i am catch in the next one  cheers  you

